# Opening a second file makes a second tab and the strip appears: a row at the top,
# one tab for each file. A tab is two cells of margin, the name, two cells, a
# closing x and a cell: "a.txt" is 5 cells and so (5 + 6) * 8 = 88 pixels wide.
# The one being edited is underlined in the accent colour, all 88 pixels of it on
# the last row of the strip; the other is on the panel's colour.
# files a.txt=A
# files b.txt=B
# open a.txt
# frames 6
# expect tabs 2 1
# expect tabnames a.txt|b.txt
# expect file b.txt
# expect text B
# pixels 88 21 176 22 232 176 74 88
# pixels 0 0 88 21 35 40 48 some
1 key o ctrl
2 text b.t
3 key enter
